WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.249
(applause)
- I dedicate this to

00:00:01.249 --> 00:00:03.003
all the indigenous kids in the world

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:06.270
who want to do art,

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:07.820
and dance, and write stories.

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:09.210
We are the original storytellers.

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:12.210
- Taika Waititi has two
feature films and a TV show

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:14.730
in the works that all
feature Maori writers.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:17.300
So let's take a look at what
exactly these projects are

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:18.500
and what we know about them

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:19.860
right now on The Ketchup.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.140
The production company
Piki Films is behind

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.717
Certified Fresh hits like
"Hunt for the Wilderpeople,"

00:00:24.717 --> 00:00:26.940
"The Breaker Upperers," and "Jojo Rabbit,"

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:28.360
and it's led by Carthew Neal

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:31.940
and Oscar-winning New Zealand
director Taika Waititi.

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:34.310
And they are now teaming
up with Maori writers

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:35.870
for projects that will mostly look at

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:37.650
the effects of colonization

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:40.154
and put indigenous voices at the center,

00:00:40.154 --> 00:00:43.250
according to reports, which is incredible.

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:46.520
The first is a feature film
adaptation of Angella Dravid's

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:49.528
award-winning stand up comedy
show, "Down the Rabbit Hole,"

00:00:49.528 --> 00:00:51.680
and it retells the comic's experience

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.190
of running away to marry a 46-year-old man

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:56.290
she met in a chat room at the age of 17,

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:59.690
before eventually landing
in a female British prison.

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:01.180
This actually happened.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:03.600
Angella is a New Zealand TV regular

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:06.000
who has been described as
a transformative comedian

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.040
with her dark and deadpan delivery.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:10.050
And it was prison where she eventually

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:11.560
and inadvertently found herself,

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:13.670
another reason why this
will be worth checking out.

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:15.190
I mean, done. Sold.

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:18.420
- I figured out how to
get a guy to call me:

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:20.300
Key his car with your phone number.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.300
- The other feature film
adaptation in the works

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:24.127
is that of Tina Makereti's novel,

00:01:24.127 --> 00:01:27.220
"The Imaginary Lives of James Poneke."

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.790
This story follows a curious Maori teen

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:32.250
who ventures to Victorian
London in the 1840s

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:35.730
to appear as a living exhibit
amongst Maori artifacts,

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:38.800
and struggles with being seen
as nothing more than a savage.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:40.387
In a statement, Makereti said,

00:01:40.387 --> 00:01:42.537
"It seems strangely
timely to see the story

00:01:42.537 --> 00:01:44.297
developed into a film as we witness

00:01:44.297 --> 00:01:47.410
the toppling of colonial
statues and attitudes."

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:49.170
And that's because, as
Variety pointed out,

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:51.560
the recent resurgence of the
Black Lives Matter movement

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:55.010
has caused a global rethink
of attitudes towards race,

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:57.500
including those related to colonization.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:59.390
And with that, the third project is

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:01.920
a television crime thriller
called "Better The Blood,"

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.510
created by Michael
Bennett and Jane Holland.

00:02:04.510 --> 00:02:06.380
Now, this will follow a Maori detective

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:08.460
as she hunts for an
indigenous serial killer

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.450
driven by the wrongs of
New Zealand's colonizers.

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:12.960
When announcing the show, Bennett said

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.460
that "this story allows us to explore

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:17.770
the long-term scars of our
brutal colonial history

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:20.377
in the context of a
visceral and popular genre."

00:02:20.377 --> 00:02:24.060
And Waititi, whose father was
a Maori farmer and artist,

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:26.460
is a great person to help
get these stories heard,

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.070
especially given how much his platform

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:30.070
has grown these past few years.

00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:30.903
I mean, who knows?

00:02:30.903 --> 00:02:32.060
Maybe we'll even get to see his face

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:33.424
in some of these movies and shows.

00:02:33.424 --> 00:02:34.950
- Hello, ladies.

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:36.920
- And since development
and production on these

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:38.190
are in the early stages,

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:39.320
we wanted to tell you guys about

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:42.200
some other Maori films
worth discovering right now,

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:45.420
which include Waititi's
2012 Certified Fresh "Boy,"

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:47.240
about an 11-year-old who gets a chance

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:49.390
to know his absentee criminal father,

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:52.150
and the 1994 movie "Once Were Warriors,"

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:53.500
about the struggles of a family

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:55.480
descended from Maori warriors,

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:58.720
and of course, 2002's
Oscar-nominated "Whale Rider,"

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:01.640
about a young Maori girl
fighting to fulfill a destiny.

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:04.015
- This will be a sacred
school of learning.

00:03:04.015 --> 00:03:06.080
You're a girl. Leave.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:07.620
- Alright friends, I want
to kick it over to you, now.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.460
Are you excited for these latest projects

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:10.810
from Taika's production company?

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:12.280
Let us know all your thoughts and feelings

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:13.113
in the comments section,

00:03:13.113 --> 00:03:15.770
and of course, for more
movie and/or streaming news,

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:17.690
head on over to RottenTomatoes.com.

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:19.410
And come find me and the
rest of the Ketchup Crew

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:20.640
in our fan group on Facebook.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:21.820
You will not regret it.

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:24.170
As always, guys, thank you so
much for watching The Ketchup.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.040
My name is Naz Perez,

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:27.210
and I hope to see your
face in the next video.

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:28.043
Bye.

00:03:28.043 --> 00:03:30.950
(upbeat funk music)

